{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjX8EXnerVud7Baa2szn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015sxAcPBXNCnMM5Ro8kUtB7","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start: clef, one-sharp key signature, then a bar with only rests (two rest signs, a full 2/4 bar). It sits just before the first bar of dotted figures, so it is bar 80. The edition's bar 80 has a D5 quarter and a quarter rest; the manuscript seems to show rests only. That is a content difference, not a bar shift. Next bar: 8th rest, A4 dotted 16th + Bb4 32nd, Bb4 8th, G4 dotted 16th + A4 32nd = bar 81. Next: F#4 8th, C#4 dotted 16th + D4 32nd, D4 8th, 8th rest = bar 82. Next: 8th rest, then high F#5 dotted + G5, G5, then C#5 dotted + D5 = bar 83. Next: D5, Bb4 dotted + A4, A4, rest = bar 84. Next: rest, A4 dotted + Bb4, Bb4, G4 dotted + A4 = bar 85 (repeats bar 81). Next: F#4, C#4 dotted + D4, D4, rests = bar 86. Last: rest, F#5 dotted + G5 32nd, G5. Then a sharped note (C#5) right at the cut edge = bar 87. Bar 88's trilled D5 is not on the line, so the line ends in bar 87.","right":true,"insights":"The dotted-rhythm figures in bars 81–87 are easy to identify. But bars 81–84 and 85–87 repeat, so the line's position rests on its first bar. That first bar shows only rests where the edition has a D5 quarter, which makes it uncertain. A clearer image of that opening bar, or the end of the line before, would settle whether it is bar 80."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5315,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5315},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"151d760f-de4c-488a-bdf